WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:04.504
- There may be a 99 arm accuracy on the line here.
- Wow.

00:00:04.754 --> 00:00:06.756
- No pressure.&nbsp;
- This is what I've been waiting for.&nbsp;

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:09.968
- [Together:] Oh!

00:00:13.096 --> 00:00:15.306
- What is up, and welcome to "Underrated,"

00:00:15.432 --> 00:00:20.103
the No. 1 show to improve athletes'
video game ratings. Behind me in the box,

00:00:20.395 --> 00:00:26.109
Nolan Arenado. Yes, eight-time Gold Glover
and just, he just smashes the ball.

00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:28.778
But we need to know how he is in The Show.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:32.157
That's why we got our pro gamer,
Ashley Sanders, to break it down.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.910
- Nolan Arenado, one of the best

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:39.873
third basemen in recent MLB history.
When it comes to his bat,

00:00:39.914 --> 00:00:43.710
he can do it all, whether it's contact,
power, drivin' in some runs,

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.253
Nolan is your guy.&nbsp;

00:00:45.253 --> 00:00:47.422
So, of course, when it comes to attributes

00:00:47.422 --> 00:00:50.592
like bunting, Nolan
Arenado is definitely underrated.

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:53.219
- Do you know what your
bunt rating is in The Show?

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:55.472
- I don't.&nbsp;
- Thirty-five.

00:00:55.472 --> 00:00:56.681
- Thirty-five.

00:00:56.681 --> 00:00:58.266
What's the highest on the bunting rating?

00:00:58.266 --> 00:01:00.435
- Probably 99.

00:01:00.477 --> 00:01:01.478
- Wow. That is low.&nbsp;

00:01:01.478 --> 00:01:05.356
- I need your ratings in The Show
for this next generation—

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.900
- Yeah.&nbsp;
- To be blown away.&nbsp;

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.943
- Yeah.&nbsp;
- And I have a guy that's gonna help us get it there.&nbsp;

00:01:08.943 --> 00:01:09.444
- All right, let's do it.

00:01:09.444 --> 00:01:11.821
- We're gonna bring in Ramone.
I'm not even gonna look at him.

00:01:11.988 --> 00:01:15.742
He's just comin' in. He's my heater in the back.
- Hey, what's happenin'? What's goin' on, man?

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:18.787
- You heard him talking about the ratings.
- Mmhmm.

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:21.247
- I wanna start off with an easy
one, his bunt rating.&nbsp;

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:21.831
- Right.

00:01:21.831 --> 00:01:23.458
- How can we take this to the next level?&nbsp;

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:25.210
And why is he at a 35?&nbsp;

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.712
- Well, cuz he doesn't bunt. He doesn't

00:01:27.712 --> 00:01:30.924
bunt. But you've got,
you got 100 on power versus

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:34.052
lefties, 99 fielding,
99 arm.

00:01:34.135 --> 00:01:35.637
Not a lotta players in the game have 99s.

00:01:35.637 --> 00:01:37.430
- Yeah.
- But, you know, everything matters.&nbsp;

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.474
You never know when you might
have to lay down that bunt.

00:01:39.682 --> 00:01:42.143
So there's nothing
better than trying to do it.

00:01:42.477 --> 00:01:44.938
- So what we've laid out
here, three targets.

00:01:45.146 --> 00:01:49.651
If you get it in that initial white
or that back blue, that's one point.

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:52.821
The sweet spot's
that middle red for two points.

00:01:52.821 --> 00:01:54.781
Anything else is minus-one.&nbsp;

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.241
And Ramone, correct me&nbsp;if I'm wrong.

00:01:56.866 --> 00:01:59.744
With 10 attempts, he could go up 20 points.&nbsp;
- He could.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.206
And that might take
you up past a 90 overall.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:06.501
So who knew that your bunt rating
could be the thing that takes you past 90 overall?

00:02:06.501 --> 00:02:07.335
- I would have never thought this—

00:02:07.335 --> 00:02:09.629
- How does that make you feel?&nbsp;
- It makes me feel really good.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:10.880
- It makes me feel—
- I really wanna lay these down.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.006
- Yes.&nbsp;
- I got this.

00:02:12.048 --> 00:02:14.384
- It's bunt time. Let's go!

00:02:14.384 --> 00:02:16.344
- All right, Nolan,
let's lay down some bunts.

00:02:16.344 --> 00:02:18.680
Start off on the first base line
whenever you're ready.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:21.224
That's a beauty.&nbsp;
- [Arenado:] OK.&nbsp;

00:02:21.224 --> 00:02:22.350
- [Lefkoe:] Sit!&nbsp;
- [Arenado:] Get in there.&nbsp;

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:23.726
- Hold on. Hold on.&nbsp;
- Is it in there? One point?

00:02:23.726 --> 00:02:26.354
- It's the first one.

00:02:26.354 --> 00:02:27.897
I think it's a one.

00:02:27.897 --> 00:02:30.775
I wanna give you the two, but I think it's a one.&nbsp;
- That's a one.

00:02:30.775 --> 00:02:32.485
- [Arenado:] I don't want handouts.
- [Lefkoe:] I gotta be honest.&nbsp;

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.779
Good speed.
- [Arenado:] No way. Same exact spot.&nbsp;

00:02:34.779 --> 00:02:35.238
- [Russell:] Same spot.
- [Lefkoe:] OK.

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:37.407
- [Arenado:] Stay fair.
- White dirt.

00:02:37.407 --> 00:02:38.241
Stay!
- Stay fair.

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:41.119
- [Russell:] Oooh. Oooh. Oooh.
- [Lefkoe:] Sit! Bang!

00:02:41.119 --> 00:02:41.911
- That's on the line.&nbsp;

00:02:41.911 --> 00:02:44.330
- [Lefkoe:] That right there is picture perfect.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:46.666
That's in there.&nbsp;That's in there.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.293
- [Russell:] That's in there.
- [Lefkoe:] That's two.&nbsp;

00:02:48.293 --> 00:02:50.003
- That's gotta go.
- [Russell:] Slow grass.&nbsp;

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:52.881
- [Lefkoe:] So two, four, five, six, seven.

00:02:53.131 --> 00:02:54.549
You're plus-seven.&nbsp;

00:02:54.549 --> 00:03:00.263
That means if you hit all of these
into the twos, we can get up to plus-17.

00:03:00.763 --> 00:03:03.474
It's on you. Hold it down, Nolan!
- Let's do it.

00:03:03.474 --> 00:03:06.728
- [Lefkoe:] All right, third base line.
- Stay fair.

00:03:06.728 --> 00:03:10.607
No! Oh, my.&nbsp;
- That's a foul. That's minus-one.

00:03:11.482 --> 00:03:14.068
OK, deep breaths. Minus-two.
It's OK.

00:03:14.152 --> 00:03:15.486
- The grass is a little high.

00:03:16.946 --> 00:03:18.740
- Get through.&nbsp;
Oh, man.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:19.324
- That's on the line.&nbsp;
- That's on&nbsp;

00:03:19.324 --> 00:03:22.452
the line, and it counts!

00:03:22.493 --> 00:03:24.329
Yeah, there it is.&nbsp;
- OK, there it is.

00:03:24.329 --> 00:03:25.872
- [Lefkoe:] That's the money shot!

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:27.498
And now the final throw.

00:03:27.498 --> 00:03:29.334
- There we go.
- And now he's got the grass.

00:03:29.459 --> 00:03:31.377
Can we do the five now?&nbsp;

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:33.922
Cuz he's got it down. Bang!

00:03:33.922 --> 00:03:35.340
Beautiful.&nbsp;
- I'll take it.&nbsp;

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.800
- All right, we went plus-seven
on the right.

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:40.386
We went plus-three on the left.

00:03:40.803 --> 00:03:41.888
That's a plus-10.&nbsp;

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:44.807
- Yep, plus-10.
- Moving him from a 35 to a 45.

00:03:45.266 --> 00:03:47.727
And you're happy to give those points?
- Happy. Happy to give those points.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.520
- Cuz you watched it happen.
&nbsp;- We watched it happen.&nbsp;

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.315
And the grass wasn't on his side.
- Plus-10, how does that feel?

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:55.735
- It feels pretty good.
I had some close calls.&nbsp;

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:58.529
My BP thrower threw great right&nbsp;
there, and I let him down a little bit.

00:03:58.529 --> 00:03:59.572
But—
- Wow.

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:00.823
- I gotta be better.
- [Together:] Team player!

00:04:00.823 --> 00:04:01.532
- Unbelievable.

00:04:03.534 --> 00:04:05.745
- Eight-time Gold Glove winner.

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:07.413
And when you look at his stats,&nbsp;

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:11.709
they match that. His fielding, his arm
strength, his reaction.

00:04:11.876 --> 00:04:17.006
All of them are top-notch for one of
the best defensive Cards in the game.

00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:21.052
However, his arm accuracy is simply

00:04:21.052 --> 00:04:24.597
just not up to par
with those other defensive attributes,

00:04:24.639 --> 00:04:28.685
which definitely makes them underrated
in that stat category.

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:38.653
- A little birdie told me that&nbsp;

00:04:38.653 --> 00:04:42.240
the arm accuracy is a little bit lower than 99.
- It's a little lower—I mean, 99, that's—

00:04:42.407 --> 00:04:44.033
- Yeah.
- You know, that's, like, perfect.&nbsp;

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:46.119
So his arm accuracy's like a [coughing] 75.&nbsp;

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:49.622
[Coughing] Seventy-five, which is great.
- I heard that through the cough.

00:04:49.664 --> 00:04:53.126
- Yeah, I know. I feel like my accuracy is OK.
I have had—my first basemans,

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:54.377
they've had to make
some good plays for me.&nbsp;

00:04:54.377 --> 00:04:55.211
There's no doubt. It's true.&nbsp;

00:04:55.211 --> 00:04:56.379
They've had to scoop
a lotta balls for me.&nbsp;

00:04:56.379 --> 00:04:57.964
There's no question about that.
- Stop being a good teammate.&nbsp;

00:04:57.964 --> 00:04:58.589
I'll talk for him.

00:04:58.589 --> 00:05:01.175
- But, but—
- That's ridiculous that he's a 75!

00:05:01.175 --> 00:05:03.344
- But I feel like I could be
higher than that.

00:05:03.511 --> 00:05:07.181
- OK. Because you said
that your first basemans have saved you,

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.184
I'm gonna be your
first baseman...kind of.

00:05:11.185 --> 00:05:13.688
And I've got a big
glove to make some big saves.

00:05:17.525 --> 00:05:19.736
This is your time&nbsp;

00:05:19.736 --> 00:05:21.571
to show us all the goods.
- Yeah.&nbsp;

00:05:21.571 --> 00:05:23.114
- We're gonna hit some balls to you down

00:05:23.114 --> 00:05:28.619
at your beautiful hot corner, the third
base, and I want you to hit the target.

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:29.746
You ready to do this?&nbsp;
- I'm ready to do it. Let's go.

00:05:29.746 --> 00:05:30.830
- Let's do it. Ramone,&nbsp;

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.499
let's go take a look. OK, Nolan.

00:05:34.083 --> 00:05:36.711
You've got this, brother.
- Ready.

00:05:39.422 --> 00:05:40.506
- [Lefkoe:] Ooh.
- [Arenado:] Oh, man.&nbsp;

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:42.759
- [Lefkoe:] I actually think it's harder to hit the pole
than it is the glove.

00:05:42.759 --> 00:05:43.134
- [Russell:] It was.&nbsp;

00:05:44.135 --> 00:05:47.472
- [Lefkoe:] Fields it. Whips it. Wow!
- Ooh. OK. Ohhh!

00:05:49.474 --> 00:05:52.060
- I hit his head! I hit his head. I got his head.

00:05:58.274 --> 00:05:59.525
- Let's up the ante.&nbsp;

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:00.735
- OK, what are you thinkin'?

00:06:00.735 --> 00:06:04.697
- You're already plus-15, maybe 20.&nbsp;
- [Lefkoe:] OK.

00:06:05.156 --> 00:06:08.534
- [Russell:] If you can hit the small glove,

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:12.455
there may be a 99
arm accuracy on the line here.

00:06:12.497 --> 00:06:13.456
- Wow.&nbsp;
- No pressure.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:14.916
- This is what I've been waiting for.

00:06:15.458 --> 00:06:17.710
That's it.&nbsp;
- That would give you 99 arm accuracy,

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.671
99 fielding and 99 arm strength.
- [Lefkoe:] Wow.

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:21.923
- [Russell:] But no pressure.&nbsp;

00:06:21.923 --> 00:06:26.969
- In the world of sports video games, there
is no number more revered than 99.

00:06:26.969 --> 00:06:27.470
- Ninety-nine.

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:29.680
And that is on the line.&nbsp;
- That is on the line.&nbsp;

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.432
- [Lefkoe:] How many throws does he get?&nbsp;
- Five.

00:06:31.432 --> 00:06:33.434
- If I can't get it in five,&nbsp;
I don't deserve it, all right?

00:06:33.434 --> 00:06:33.768
- Let's get it.

00:06:33.768 --> 00:06:38.147
- A 99 on the line, feelin' fine.
- Ninety-nine arm accuracy is on the line.

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:47.073
- Round 2. Oh!
- Oooh.&nbsp;

00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:52.286
- [Together:] Oh!
- Oh, my gosh.

00:06:52.787 --> 00:06:55.498
- Like 12 inches too low.&nbsp;

00:06:57.875 --> 00:07:00.962
- No!

00:07:00.962 --> 00:07:01.879
- [Russell:] There it is.&nbsp;

00:07:02.755 --> 00:07:03.131
- Last one?&nbsp;

00:07:03.131 --> 00:07:04.590
- Last one.&nbsp;
- OK.&nbsp;

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.342
All right, hold on. Hold on.
- If I don't get it, I don't deserve it.

00:07:06.342 --> 00:07:07.552
- Let's take a break.
- That's what it comes down to.

00:07:08.386 --> 00:07:09.011
- Take a break.

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:10.304
- Here it is.&nbsp;
- All right, last one. Ready?

00:07:10.304 --> 00:07:11.973
- For 99, feelin' fine.

00:07:18.813 --> 00:07:22.316
- No way!&nbsp;
- I thought that went between my face and the glove.

00:07:22.358 --> 00:07:25.069
- I think it did.&nbsp;
- [Lefkoe:] It's OK. It's OK.

00:07:25.695 --> 00:07:27.029
This is why it's—
- [Arenado:] That's all I got.

00:07:27.029 --> 00:07:29.490
- [Lefkoe:] This is why I appreciate Nolan.&nbsp;

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:31.617
What I'm feeling, the energy out of you right now

00:07:31.826 --> 00:07:33.327
is you're a little bit disappointed.&nbsp;

00:07:33.327 --> 00:07:35.496
We went into that final throw plus-15.

00:07:35.663 --> 00:07:38.249
So he's a 90 arm accuracy.&nbsp;

00:07:38.249 --> 00:07:40.084
What is this gonna do&nbsp;
to his overall rating?&nbsp;

00:07:40.084 --> 00:07:41.794
- It's probably gonna bump him to a 90.

00:07:43.963 --> 00:07:46.591
- How ya feelin'? We're
looking at the replays right now.

00:07:46.799 --> 00:07:48.551
You're, like, an inch away.&nbsp;
- [Arenado:] Yeah. Yeah.

00:07:48.551 --> 00:07:49.594
- [Lefkoe:] That last one...

00:07:50.094 --> 00:07:53.181
- [Arenado:] I mean, I feel good about it,
but I still, I feel a little disappointed.&nbsp;

00:07:53.389 --> 00:07:54.682
A little bad time, yeah.

00:07:54.682 --> 00:07:57.018
I mean, I swear that
went right through your head and the glove.

00:07:58.561 --> 00:08:01.439
- There's part of me that's OK that you didn't bust up the face.
- [Laughing]

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:02.899
- It's a big day.&nbsp;
- It's a big day.

00:08:03.191 --> 00:08:04.108
- Bunts went up.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:07.069
Throwing accuracy now a 90.
- Yeah.

00:08:07.069 --> 00:08:08.279
- MLB The Show.
- Yeah.

00:08:08.279 --> 00:08:11.240
- Do you have a message for all the gamers out
there that are thinking about using you?

00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:13.993
- Well, if you wanna lay down
a bunt in a big situation, I got you.

00:08:14.452 --> 00:08:17.038
And I'm gonna make my plays for you guys. I promise.&nbsp;
- You're the man.

00:08:17.246 --> 00:08:19.165
- Yeah, appreciate you boys.
- Appreciate you, man.&nbsp;

00:08:19.165 --> 00:08:22.084
I don't like that you smashed my face,
but I did find it entertaining.

00:08:22.293 --> 00:08:23.419
So that was good.&nbsp;
- That was awesome.

